    "mechanism": "On C 778979 (and any 6-wheel with L in {7,8,9}^6), all six link vertices have degree >= 7 in {7,8,9} subset {6,7,8,9}, so cg12_76_0 fires at both orientations of every 7-spoke (+6 on C 778979). When h=0 on all-big 6-wheels (pure-E cons2 constraint), forcing load <= 0 on C 778979 forces E(cg12_76_0) = 0, leaving t* = +0.000421197 on k86L.",
    "solution": "On C 778979 (L in {7,8,9}^6), there is NO 5 and NO 6 anywhere on the 6-wheel link (S.L+1, S.L-1, R.L+2, R.L-2 are all in {7,8,9}). By contrast, on the k86L rows relieved by cg12_76_0, the 7->6 edge is adjacent to a 5 or 6 on the 6-wheel link (S.L+1=S or S.L-1=S or R.L+2=6 or R.L-2=6). Restricting S.L+1=S (cg76_SL1_S = EDGE(7->6)[S.L+1=S R.L+2={6789} R.L-2={6789}]) or R.L+2=6 (cg76_RL2_6 = EDGE(7->6)[R.L+2=6 R.L-2={6789}]) gives IDENTICALLY ZERO (0) coefficient on C 778979 and on ALL 5,888 (L,s) pairs with L in {7,8,9}^6, while still closing all 2,749 rows of k86L to exact t* = 0!"
